<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>Where the golden sands of the Gobi meet the emerald rice terraces of Yunnan — this 16-day journey is China's ultimate contrast tour. Start on the ancient Silk Road through Dunhuang, Turpan, and Kashgar, then fly south to Yunnan, the "Land of Eternal Spring." From the Mogao Caves to Lijiang's cobblestone alleys, from camel rides to tea ceremonies, this tour captures China's staggering diversity in one seamless adventure.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Mogao Caves — 1,000 years of Buddhist art</li><li>Camel ride at Singing Sand Dunes</li>
      <li>Kashgar's Sunday Bazaar</li>
      <li>Karakoram Highway to Karakul Lake</li>
      <li>Stone Forest — Kunming's karst wonderland</li>
      <li>Cycle around Erhai Lake in Dali</li>
      <li>Lijiang Old Town — UNESCO world heritage</li>
      <li>Shangri-La — the mythical Tibetan paradise</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Dunhuang</h4><p>Fly into Dunhuang, the gateway to the Silk Road's greatest treasure. Airport transfer, hotel check-in. Evening stroll through Shazhou Night Market. Try local specialties: donkey meat noodles and apricot tea.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Dunhuang 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang — Mogao Caves & Singing Sand Dunes</h4><p>Full UNESCO World Heritage day. Morning at the Mogao Caves — 492 grottoes with 45,000 sqm of Buddhist murals spanning 1,000 years. Afternoon: camel ride across the Singing Sand Dunes to Crescent Moon Spring at sunset.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Dunhuang 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang &#8594; Turpan (High-speed train)</h4><p>Morning at Yumen Pass and the Han Dynasty Great Wall ruins. Afternoon high-speed train to Turpan (4 hrs). Arrive in China's hottest city, 154m below sea level.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Turpan 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan — Flaming Mountains & Grape Valley</h4><p>Visit Jiaohe Ancient City — the world's best-preserved earthen city. Marvel at the Karez irrigation system, an engineering wonder. Afternoon: wander through Grape Valley's shaded vineyards. Evening Uyghur dance show.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Turpan 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan &#8594; Urumqi &#9992; Kashgar</h4><p>Morning drive to Urumqi, visit the Xinjiang Museum to see 3,800-year-old Tarim mummies. Afternoon flight to Kashgar — the legendary crossroads of the Silk Road.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Sunday Bazaar & Old City</h4><p>The iconic Sunday Bazaar — thousands of traders, camels, carpets, and spices. Afternoon: explore the Old City's mud-brick alleys. Visit Id Kah Mosque. Evening tea at a century-old teahouse with Uyghur musicians.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Karakoram Highway to Karakul Lake</h4><p>Drive the legendary Karakoram Highway to Karakul Lake (3,600m). Panoramic views of Muztagh Ata (7,546m) and Kongur Tagh (7,649m). Visit Kyrgyz nomad settlements along the lake.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar &#8594; Abakh Khoja Tomb &#9992; Kunming</h4><p>Morning visit to Abakh Khoja Tomb — the "Fragrant Concubine's" mausoleum. Afternoon flight to Kunming, Yunnan. The climate shift from desert to spring-like weather is dramatic!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kunming 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kunming — Stone Forest</h4><p>Day trip to the Stone Forest — a UNESCO karst landscape of towering limestone pinnacles, sacred to the Yi people. Afternoon: Green Lake Park and Yunnan cuisine (Across-the-Bridge Noodles).</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kunming 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kunming &#128646; Dali (High-speed train)</h4><p>Morning bullet train to Dali (2 hrs). Afternoon: explore Dali Old Town — cobblestone streets, traditional Bai architecture, and the iconic Three Pagodas reflected in the water. Sunset at Erhai Lake.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Dali 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>11</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dali — Erhai Lake Cycling & Xizhou Village</h4><p>Morning bicycle ride around Erhai Lake (20 km, flat, easy). Visit Xizhou Bai Village for traditional tie-dye workshop and three-course tea ceremony. Afternoon free to explore.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Dali 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>12</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dali &#8594; Lijiang</h4><p>Drive to Lijiang (2.5 hrs) through terraced farmland. Afternoon: explore Lijiang Old Town — a UNESCO site of cobblestone alleys, wooden bridges, and flowing canals. Night view from Lion Hill.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Lijiang 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>13</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Lijiang — Jade Dragon Snow Mountain</h4><p>Full day at Jade Dragon Snow Mountain. Cable car to 4,506m for views of 13 peaks and glaciers. Watch Zhang Yimou's "Impression Lijiang" outdoor performance. Afternoon: Baisha murals and Naxi villages.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Lijiang 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>14</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Lijiang &#8594; Tiger Leaping Gorge &#8594; Shangri-La</h4><p>Drive to Tiger Leaping Gorge — one of the world's deepest river canyons. Hike a section of the high trail for breathtaking views. Continue to Shangri-La (Zhongdian) at 3,200m.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Shangri-La 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>15</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Shangri-La — Tibetan Paradise</h4><p>Visit Songzanlin Monastery — the "Little Potala Palace." Explore Dukezong Ancient Town with its giant prayer wheel. Afternoon: Pudacuo National Park — pristine lakes, meadows, and forests. Farewell Tibetan hotpot dinner.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Shangri-La 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>16</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart from Shangri-La or Lijiang</h4><p>Airport transfer to Diqing Shangri-La Airport or return to Lijiang for departure. From the Gobi Desert to Tibetan Shangri-La — what a journey! &#20877;&#35265;!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127860; B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

